# No scattered pricing

Rates, currency amounts, indicative totals, “from ₹/£/$…”, per-night figures, and rate-validity dates appear **only** on a dedicated pricing surface: tariff card, price list, pricing page, or handbook tariff section.

They do not appear on home, programme, enquiry, journal, app, component demos, type specimens, or marketing copy. Changing a rate must never require a repo-wide hunt.

## Allowed

- `ui_kits/website/screens/TariffScreen.js` (the website tariff card), which in this design system shows the structure with “—” only. No real figure is stored in this repo.
- Brand-deck slides whose subject *is* rooms & tariffs
- The Property Handbook tariff section
- A future page whose filename/title is clearly a price list / tariff / pricing document

## Not allowed

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — price on a programme, card, or home teaser
<p>90 min · from {price}</p>
<span>₹{room.single} / night</span>
<div>₹{(room.single * nights).toLocaleString("en-IN")}</div>

// ✅ GOOD — point at the tariff card
<Button onClick={() => onNavigate("tariffs")}>View the tariff card</Button>
```

## Also forbidden outside those surfaces

- Inventing or repeating a rate as a “placeholder” or type sample
- Embedding ₹ / $ / £ amounts in `i18n.js` keys used by non-tariff screens
- Calculating stay totals on enquiry or programme panels

Link to the tariff card. Do not quote it.